00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:39,333
The Woman in Black is a 1989 British horror drama television film directed by Herbert Wise
and starring Adrian Rawlins, Bernard Hepton, David Daker and Pauline Moran.

11
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
The teleplay is adapted from the 1983 novel of the same name by Susan Hill.

12
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
It focuses on a young solicitor who is sent to a coastal English village to
settle the estate of a reclusive widow, and finds the town haunted.

13
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
The programme was produced by Central Independent Television
for ITV, and premiered on Christmas Eve 1989.

14
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
It was an unexpected success, though author Susan Hill reportedly disagreed with some
of the slight changes screenwriter Nigel Kneale made in the adaptation.

15
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
Another film version, starring Daniel Radcliffe, was released in 2012.

